{#
  Template for the Visual Storytelling block reference documentation page.
  Variables:
  - blocks: array of block definition arrays, each with keys:
      id, label, description, use_for, fields (assoc), tips
#}
<div class="vs-docs">

  <div class="vs-docs__header">
    <p class="vs-docs__intro">Use these blocks on any <strong>Flex Page</strong> to build Shorthand-style stories. Add blocks through the Layout Builder browser — the Visual Storytelling category holds all ten block types documented here.</p>
    <nav class="vs-docs__toc" aria-label="Block list">
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#vs-block-publishing-and-tags">Publishing &amp; Tagging</a></li>
        {% for block in blocks %}
          <li><a href="#vs-block-{{ block.id }}">{{ block.label }}</a></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <section class="vs-docs__block" id="vs-block-publishing-and-tags">
    <div class="vs-docs__block-header">
      <h2 class="vs-docs__block-name">Publishing &amp; Tagging Your Story</h2>
      <p class="vs-docs__block-desc">A story page (Flex Page) has no tags field of its own. To make a story discoverable — including tagging it for Bridging Barriers (BB) — publish a short companion News article that links out to it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="vs-docs__fields">
      <h3>Steps</h3>
      <dl>
        <dt>1. Build &amp; publish the story</dt>
        <dd>Finish your story page in Story Builder and publish it. Copy its URL.</dd>
        <dt>2. Create a companion News article</dt>
        <dd>Go to Content &gt; Add content &gt; News. Give it a title, and leave the Body field empty (it won't be shown).</dd>
        <dt>3. Set the External link</dt>
        <dd>Paste the story's URL into the News article's <strong>External link</strong> field. This makes the article's title link straight to your story instead of a separate News page.</dd>
        <dt>4. Add News tags</dt>
        <dd>Tag every story's companion article with the existing <strong>Visual Story</strong> News tag so all stories can be found as a group. For Bridging Barriers stories, also add a <strong>Bridging Barriers</strong> tag (create it once under Structure &gt; Taxonomy &gt; News tags — it doesn't exist yet).</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="vs-docs__tips">
      <h3>Tips</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The News article is just a pointer — most of its own fields (body, image, etc.) can stay blank once the External link is set.</li>
        <li>The News RSS feed currently links to the News article itself rather than the external story URL; everything else (listing blocks, listing pages) follows the External link correctly.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  {% for block in blocks %}
    <section class="vs-docs__block" id="vs-block-{{ block.id }}">
      <div class="vs-docs__block-header">
        <h2 class="vs-docs__block-name">{{ block.label }}</h2>
        <p class="vs-docs__block-desc">{{ block.description }}</p>
        {% if block.use_for %}
          <ul class="vs-docs__use-for">
            {% for use in block.use_for %}
              <li>{{ use }}</li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

      {% if block.example %}
        <div class="vs-docs__example-wrap">
          <div class="vs-docs__example-label">Example</div>
          <div class="vs-docs__example" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="vs-docs__example-inner">
              {{ block.example }}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% if block.fields %}
        <div class="vs-docs__fields">
          <h3>Fields</h3>
          <dl>
            {% for field_name, field_desc in block.fields %}
              <dt>{{ field_name }}</dt>
              <dd>{{ field_desc }}</dd>
            {% endfor %}
          </dl>
        </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% if block.tips %}
        <div class="vs-docs__tips">
          <h3>Tips</h3>
          <ul>
            {% for tip in block.tips %}
              <li>{{ tip }}</li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
      {% endif %}
    </section>
  {% endfor %}

</div>
